1
00:02:48,877 --> 00:02:51,504
Hello , Matthew . What are you doing here so late ?

2
00:02:51,755 --> 00:02:52,880
I came to get the books .

3
00:02:53,131 --> 00:02:54,507
I want to study our accounts .

4
00:02:54,758 --> 00:02:56,592
We 've been doing very well lately .

5
00:02:56,844 --> 00:02:59,053
Over 200 paid admissions today .

6
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:01,430
You call that good Saturday business ?

7
00:03:01,682 --> 00:03:04,475
If you weren 't so stubborn , we 'd be turning them away from here .

8
00:03:05,185 --> 00:03:07,436
Who cares a hang about history in wax ?

9
00:03:07,688 --> 00:03:10,022
There are people in the world who love beauty .

10
00:03:10,274 --> 00:03:12,608
But more who want sensation , shock !

11
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:16,112
The morbidly curious . Heh , I won 't cater to them .

12
00:03:16,363 --> 00:03:18,781
Their money is as good as anybody else 's .

13
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:21,951
You should have seen them turning them away at that wax museum

14
00:03:22,202 --> 00:03:24,954
on 23rd Street - the Eden Musée .

15
00:03:25,205 --> 00:03:27,665
The story 's the same at Madame Tussaud 's in London .

16
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:30,418
- If you 'd only listened to me- - - I know , Matthew .

17
00:03:30,669 --> 00:03:34,714
murder , torture , executions

18
00:03:34,965 --> 00:03:38,259
scare the living daylights out of people . I don 't care for that kind of patronage .

19
00:03:38,510 --> 00:03:40,511
You 're a great artist , a genius sculptor .

20
00:03:40,762 --> 00:03:44,140
But I 'm an ordinary businessman . I want a quick return on my investment .

21
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:47,393
I 've got $ 20,000 sunk in this historic peep show of yours .

22
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:49,061
I could use that money to better advantage .

23
00:03:49,313 --> 00:03:51,188
All right , Matthew . All right .

24
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:54,859
I 've known for some time you wanted to dissolve our partnership .

25
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:56,986
I think I may be able to accommodate you .

26
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:58,154
How ?

27
00:03:58,405 --> 00:04:02,241
A friend is bringing Sidney Wallace , the art critic , here tonight to see my work .

28
00:04:02,492 --> 00:04:07,079
Wallace is rich , and I think I might persuade him to buy you out .

29
00:04:07,331 --> 00:04:09,248
Well , that sounds interesting .

30
00:04:09,499 --> 00:04:11,125
I 'll want a profit on my investment .

31
00:04:11,376 --> 00:04:12,543
Yes , Matthew .

32
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:14,211
I understand .

33
00:04:14,463 --> 00:04:16,631
You leave everything to me , and I promise you it will be- -

34
00:04:18,467 --> 00:04:19,717
That should be they now .

35
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:21,302
All right , I 'll wait in the office .

36
00:04:21,553 --> 00:04:23,429
I 've heard of Wallace . He has a pot of money .

37
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,598
If he likes your stuff , put a stiff price on it .

38
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:41,822
- Does Jarrod live in the building ? - Yes , he has a room upstairs .

39
00:04:42,074 --> 00:04:45,201
You 'll like him , Sidney . He speaks your language .

40
00:04:45,911 --> 00:04:48,287
Please come in . I 'm happy to see you , Bruce .

41
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:50,790
It was such a bad night I was afraid you couldn 't get here .

42
00:04:51,041 --> 00:04:53,292
We were delayed . He had a meeting at Manhattan Gallery .

43
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:55,211
My friend Sidney Wallace . Professor Jarrod .

44
00:04:55,462 --> 00:04:57,213
- It 's a great pleasure . - For me also .

45
00:04:57,464 --> 00:05:00,341
That 's a title that was bestowed on me when I became an exhibitor .

46
00:05:00,592 --> 00:05:02,510
It has little to do with my real work .

47
00:05:02,761 --> 00:05:05,429
If you 'll come with me , I 'll show you what that work is .

48
00:05:05,681 --> 00:05:07,765
I 'm afraid the visit of such a distinguished critic

49
00:05:08,016 --> 00:05:09,976
may cause my children to become conceited .

50
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:14,480
To you , they 're wax . But to me , their creator , they live and breathe .

51
00:05:14,731 --> 00:05:17,608
Here we have two great lovers from the past .

52
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:22,363
Cleopatra , queen of Egypt , and Mark Antony . Their last meeting .

53
00:05:22,614 --> 00:05:25,491
You 'll recall that Antony , believing Cleopatra to be dead

54
00:05:25,742 --> 00:05:27,493
killed himself with his own sword .

55
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:30,955
When Cleopatra discovered what happened , she quickly followed her lover .

56
00:05:31,206 --> 00:05:33,833
You noticed how cleverly the hair is mounted on the scalp ?

57
00:05:34,084 --> 00:05:35,418
Yes . How do you do that , professor ?

58
00:05:35,669 --> 00:05:38,838
Well , real hair of the proper color and texture

59
00:05:39,089 --> 00:05:41,924
is pressed into the slightly warmed wax with a scalpel

60
00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:43,467
one hair at a time .

61
00:05:43,719 --> 00:05:47,513
Each wave and curl of the subject 's own hair is reproduced .

62
00:05:53,228 --> 00:05:56,897
Here 's President Lincoln and his assassin , John Wilkes Booth

63
00:05:57,149 --> 00:05:59,984
one of my few concessions to the macabre .

64
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:03,821
That 's the best figure of Booth I 've seen . You almost expect him to speak .

65
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:05,990
I wonder what he 'd say after all these years .

66
00:06:06,241 --> 00:06:07,742
I 'm sure he 'd rant a bit .

67
00:06:07,993 --> 00:06:11,495
Even after he shot Lincoln and jumped from the President 's box onto the stage

68
00:06:11,747 --> 00:06:14,623
he couldn 't resist turning to the audience and taking a bow .

69
00:06:14,875 --> 00:06:16,917
I found him a very stubborn person .

70
00:06:17,169 --> 00:06:18,419
- Stubborn ? - Unbelievably .

71
00:06:18,670 --> 00:06:22,798
For days I argued with this fellow before I could get him to pose the way I wanted him to .

72
00:06:23,050 --> 00:06:25,468
- You mean , he talked back to you ? - Of course .

73
00:06:25,719 --> 00:06:28,012
It 's not easy to shut an actor 's mouth .

74
00:06:28,722 --> 00:06:32,683
These groups are like dimensional paintings of the old masters .

75
00:06:32,934 --> 00:06:34,060
This is not only a great show

76
00:06:34,311 --> 00:06:35,311
it 's an art exhibit .

77
00:06:35,562 --> 00:06:36,687
That 's what I told you .

78
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,232
Here we have Joan of Arc

79
00:06:40,484 --> 00:06:42,068
a favorite subject of mine .

80
00:06:42,319 --> 00:06:44,153
I can understand . It 's beautifully done .

81
00:06:44,404 --> 00:06:45,362
Thank you .

82
00:06:45,614 --> 00:06:49,492
I 've done her over a dozen times , haven 't I , my dear ? And still she doesn 't complain .

83
00:06:49,743 --> 00:06:52,828
- What was wrong with her ? - There are no authentic portraits available

84
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:55,873
so sculptors and painters have to work from models .

85
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:58,459
I 've never found the right one , but I will one of these days .

86
00:06:58,710 --> 00:07:00,419
It 's a shame to race through such an exhibit .

87
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,588
One should have time to really study these figures .

88
00:07:02,839 --> 00:07:06,300
You 're very kind . My creations have some merit , I suspect

89
00:07:06,551 --> 00:07:09,428
but in bringing back to life the lovely Marie Antoinette

90
00:07:09,679 --> 00:07:11,555
I feel I 've done my best work .

91
00:07:11,807 --> 00:07:13,891
Ah , I 've never seen anything so exquisite .

92
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:16,811
People say they can see my Marie Antoinette breathe

93
00:07:17,062 --> 00:07:19,146
that her breast rises and falls .

94
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:22,024
Look at her eyes , they follow you wherever you go .

95
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:24,318
She 's very real to me .

96
00:07:25,028 --> 00:07:26,904
You know , her eyes do follow you .

97
00:07:27,155 --> 00:07:28,656
They 're made of glass , more 's the pity .

98
00:07:28,907 --> 00:07:31,200
The exact size and color of the original .

99
00:07:31,451 --> 00:07:34,578
They 're inserted into the sockets from inside

100
00:07:34,830 --> 00:07:37,998
by way of the hollow neck , before the head is attached to the body .

101
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:42,294
Forgive me , my dear , for discussing your intimate secrets .

102
00:07:42,546 --> 00:07:45,589
I 'm sorry . I lose myself at times .

103
00:07:45,841 --> 00:07:48,592
Professor , if people knew what you have inside these walls

104
00:07:48,844 --> 00:07:51,011
you couldn 't accommodate the crowds .

105
00:07:51,263 --> 00:07:54,014
What you need here is exploitation , more advertising .

106
00:07:54,266 --> 00:07:57,017
- That 's what I 've been telling him . - Oh , my partner wouldn 't agree .

107
00:07:57,269 --> 00:07:58,144
He 's not happy here .

108
00:07:58,395 --> 00:08:01,230
He wants to invest in something else . Mr. Wallace

109
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:05,401
would you become a partner in this venture ? Would you buy him out ?

110
00:08:05,652 --> 00:08:09,280
You know , I might take you up on that if my lawyers approve and the price is right .

111
00:08:09,531 --> 00:08:12,116
With your support , I could do wonders . I 'd make any sacrifice .

112
00:08:12,367 --> 00:08:14,243
Unfortunately , I 'm leaving this weekend for Egypt .

113
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:16,162
I 'm financing some excavations there .

114
00:08:16,413 --> 00:08:18,706
However , I 'll be back in three months , then I 'll discuss- -

115
00:08:18,957 --> 00:08:20,583
You make me very happy .

116
00:08:20,834 --> 00:08:24,086
You intrigue me , professor . I believe we 'd get along together .

117
00:08:24,337 --> 00:08:25,838
- Good night . - Good night .

118
00:08:26,089 --> 00:08:28,007
- And I 'm grateful to you , Bruce . - Oh , it 's all right .

119
00:08:32,846 --> 00:08:35,222
Thank you both for your visit and your encouragement .

120
00:08:35,473 --> 00:08:37,391
- I 'll probably see you in three months . - Good night .

121
00:08:37,642 --> 00:08:38,601
Good night .

122
00:08:52,991 --> 00:08:56,410
Mr. Wallace is a great art critic , my darling . You heard what he said .

123
00:08:56,661 --> 00:08:58,287
Does he make you happy ?

124
00:08:58,538 --> 00:09:01,290
Of course you 'd say that . But I don 't care about success .

125
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:04,251
The world will acknowledge your beauty .

126
00:09:04,502 --> 00:09:06,003
And you , my friends

127
00:09:06,254 --> 00:09:09,548
Cleopatra , Mark Antony , Lincoln , Joan of Arc , all of you .

128
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:11,425
How would it suit you to be famous again ?

129
00:09:13,511 --> 00:09:16,430
I know it 'll please you , you conceited devil .

130
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:19,892
It was like you to get yourself shot down in a burning barn .

131
00:09:20,143 --> 00:09:22,853
Couldn 't do it without a spotlight , could you ?

132
00:09:23,104 --> 00:09:25,814
Do you really hear what they say , Jarrod ?

133
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:27,358
Of course .

134
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:33,572
A man has to be a little nuts to be a good showman .

135
00:09:33,823 --> 00:09:35,824
The sooner I 'm out of it , the better .

136
00:09:36,076 --> 00:09:37,660
You 'll be out soon , Matthew .

137
00:09:37,911 --> 00:09:40,037
Mr. Wallace returns from Egypt in three months .

138
00:09:40,288 --> 00:09:41,914
He 'll be ready to talk business then .

139
00:09:42,165 --> 00:09:44,708
- I heard him . That 's no good for me . - But surely you don 't- -

140
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:46,418
I have a chance to buy in on something .

141
00:09:46,670 --> 00:09:48,921
It 'll pay off in a big way and three months is too late .

142
00:09:49,172 --> 00:09:51,715
What guarantee do I have that he won 't go cold on the deal ?

143
00:09:51,967 --> 00:09:54,927
- Sorry , Matthew . It 's the best I could do . - I can do better .

144
00:09:55,679 --> 00:09:58,347
How would you like to split $ 25,000 with me ?

145
00:09:58,598 --> 00:10:00,099
And you call me crazy ?

146
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:03,352
You ever thought of what would happen if we had a fire here ?

147
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:06,605
In the cellar , there are six barrels of wax . Wax has a paraffin base .

148
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:10,150
It 's highly inflammable . This whole place would go up like a paint factory .

149
00:10:10,402 --> 00:10:12,987
Burn ? Burn all my people ?

150
00:10:13,238 --> 00:10:15,281
- Do you think I 'm a murderer ? - Oh , stop dreaming .

151
00:10:15,532 --> 00:10:19,576
These dummies are insured for $ 25,000 . That 's $ 12,500 for each of us .

152
00:10:19,953 --> 00:10:22,246
You wouldn 't need Wallace . You 'd have enough to begin again .

153
00:10:22,497 --> 00:10:25,124
No , I 'd rather die myself than see my friends destroyed .

154
00:10:25,375 --> 00:10:27,584
I won 't Let you do it , and I 'll kill you if you try .

155
00:10:27,836 --> 00:10:29,169
Don 't be stupid .

156
00:10:29,421 --> 00:10:33,048
All you have to do is to strike a match and the thing is done .

157
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:36,495
Yes , my friend was a genius .

158
00:16:36,746 --> 00:16:38,455
A great artist .

159
00:16:38,706 --> 00:16:41,291
Only I could understand him .

160
00:16:41,542 --> 00:16:44,169
We were like that , Cathy . Just like that .

161
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:48,131
- Couldn 't they ever find him after the fire ? - Not a sign of him .

162
00:16:48,383 --> 00:16:52,344
The place burned like a paint fac- - Like a volcano .

163
00:16:52,595 --> 00:16:55,180
He was such an impractical fellow .

164
00:16:55,431 --> 00:16:57,349
But I still loved him .

165
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:59,810
And had I been there , I might have saved him .

166
00:17:00,061 --> 00:17:02,479
Oh , but you might have gotten burned yourself , Matty .

167
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:04,606
Yes . Such is life .

168
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:07,651
No matter how much we lose , we must still go on living .

169
00:17:07,902 --> 00:17:12,239
Was there- - ? Was there any insurance on the wax museum ?

170
00:17:12,490 --> 00:17:15,242
Yes , I- - I had a little difficulty about that .

171
00:17:15,493 --> 00:17:18,078
According to the terms of the partnership agreement

172
00:17:18,329 --> 00:17:20,706
the money was to go to the survivor of the others .

173
00:17:20,957 --> 00:17:24,167
The insurance company insists upon proof of , uh , my partner 's death .

174
00:17:24,419 --> 00:17:25,085
Yes .

175
00:17:25,336 --> 00:17:27,713
Hee , hee . They always want a corpse .

176
00:17:27,964 --> 00:17:30,924
But they settled finally . This afternoon , as a matter of fact .

177
00:17:31,175 --> 00:17:31,842
They didn 't !

178
00:17:32,093 --> 00:17:33,051
Certified check .

179
00:17:33,302 --> 00:17:35,887
I got it cashed . The money is in my safe .

180
00:17:36,139 --> 00:17:39,307
- You know what that means , baby ? - No , what ?

181
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:41,351
That little trip I was talking to you about ... ?

182
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:44,980
Ooh , Matty . Heh .

183
00:17:45,231 --> 00:17:47,983
- You 're such a card ! - Ha-ha-ha .

184
00:17:48,234 --> 00:17:51,278
- How much did you get ? - $ 25,000 .

185
00:17:51,529 --> 00:17:54,072
- Where would you like to go ? Atlantic City ?

186
00:17:54,323 --> 00:17:59,077
No . Niagara Falls . We can get the license in Buffalo .

187
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:02,956
- License ? - Yeah , you know .

188
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:04,708
Legitimate .

189
00:18:06,252 --> 00:18:07,878
Ah , why not ? It might be fun .

190
00:18:08,129 --> 00:18:09,880
Uh , waiter ? Waiter , my check .

191
00:21:15,608 --> 00:21:18,193
Pull it tighter , Sue .

192
00:21:19,612 --> 00:21:21,947
Pull it tighter .

193
00:21:22,949 --> 00:21:24,491
I want a waist like Anna Held .

194
00:21:24,742 --> 00:21:27,869
If I pull it any tighter , you 're not going to be able to breathe .

195
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,996
Oh . Oh , that 's all right .

196
00:21:30,247 --> 00:21:32,457
I don 't need much breath , anyway .

197
00:21:32,708 --> 00:21:35,126
As my late friend Matty used to say :

198
00:21:35,378 --> 00:21:37,629
" If a girl don 't watch her figure , the men won 't . "

199
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:40,715
Matty . Wasn 't that the man you were going to marry ?

200
00:21:40,967 --> 00:21:42,801
Yes , but he hung himself instead .

201
00:21:44,345 --> 00:21:46,638
Oh , Matty was such a card .

202
00:21:46,889 --> 00:21:48,974
Where is your new friend gonna take you tonight ?

203
00:21:49,225 --> 00:21:50,308
The Hoffman House for dinner .

204
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:53,103
And then to Tony Pastor 's for the vaudeville show .

205
00:21:53,354 --> 00:21:56,439
- That sounds like fun . - He 's a free spender , all right .

206
00:21:56,691 --> 00:21:59,693
Little bit older than I like them , but awfully distinguished looking .

207
00:21:59,944 --> 00:22:00,610
Is he nice ?

208
00:22:00,861 --> 00:22:02,278
Oh , awfully nice .

209
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:05,156
A real gentleman , except when he 's had a couple of drinks in him .

210
00:22:06,784 --> 00:22:08,243
Ah , that 's to be expected .

211
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:10,245
I 'm moving up- -

212
00:22:10,496 --> 00:22:13,331
Ooh . I 'm moving up in the world , honey .

213
00:22:13,582 --> 00:22:16,584
No girl ever hits the jackpot till after she passes 14th Street .

214
00:22:16,836 --> 00:22:19,129
- Ha , ha , is that how it goes ? - Sure .

215
00:22:19,797 --> 00:22:21,715
Oh . Look at me .

216
00:22:21,966 --> 00:22:24,217
Not too long ago , I was down on Delancey Street .

217
00:22:24,468 --> 00:22:28,013
And tonight I 'll be right up there among the bright lights on 23rd .

218
00:22:28,264 --> 00:22:30,724
Now , when you get up there tonight , don 't drink too much .

219
00:22:30,975 --> 00:22:32,642
Oh , don 't worry , I won 't .

220
00:22:32,893 --> 00:22:37,480
He keeps trying to pour the liquor into me , but I always manage to keep my head .

221
00:22:37,732 --> 00:22:41,276
After all , now that I 'm going regular with a swell

222
00:22:41,527 --> 00:22:43,737
I got social obligations . Ha , ha .

223
00:22:43,988 --> 00:22:48,033
You know how it is when a fella- - Ah , no , of course you don 't know .

224
00:22:48,284 --> 00:22:50,994
You 're not like me , Sue . You never could be .

225
00:22:51,245 --> 00:22:53,872
You got all the brains and all I 've got is

226
00:22:55,291 --> 00:22:56,666
what I got .

227
00:22:56,917 --> 00:22:58,877
You know , I 'm surprised you even talk to me .

228
00:22:59,128 --> 00:23:01,588
That 's such nonsense . You 've been so good to me .

229
00:23:01,839 --> 00:23:02,922
Oh , why not ?

230
00:23:03,174 --> 00:23:05,925
A girl needs a friend when she 's down on her luck .

231
00:23:06,177 --> 00:23:09,512
Holy smoke ! Look at the time . I 've got to hurry .

232
00:23:09,764 --> 00:23:10,930
Did you find a job yet ?

233
00:23:11,182 --> 00:23:14,684
Oh , no , not yet , but they need a hat-check girl at the Silver Slipper

234
00:23:14,935 --> 00:23:17,020
and I 've got an appointment with the manager tonight .

235
00:23:17,271 --> 00:23:19,397
Oh , I know that fellow . Watch out for him .

236
00:23:19,648 --> 00:23:22,734
- But why ? What 's the matter with him ? - Oh , nothing much .

237
00:23:22,985 --> 00:23:25,403
- Long as you know how to duck . - Oh , that kind ?

238
00:23:25,654 --> 00:23:26,654
Yes .

239
00:23:26,906 --> 00:23:29,407
- Did you eat today ? - Uh-huh . I had everything I needed .

240
00:23:29,658 --> 00:23:31,201
To hear you tell it .

241
00:23:31,452 --> 00:23:33,536
Besides , you 're behind in your room rent .

242
00:23:33,788 --> 00:23:35,705
Oh , well , Mrs. Flannigan will wait for me .

243
00:23:35,956 --> 00:23:37,123
Don 't count on that .

244
00:23:37,374 --> 00:23:40,376
The old buzzard almost locked me out once .

245
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:41,920
There .

246
00:23:42,171 --> 00:23:44,380
If I don 't sizzle him tonight , I might as well give up .

247
00:23:45,883 --> 00:23:47,217
He 's picking me up in a hansom cab .

248
00:23:47,468 --> 00:23:50,428
No trolley for him . He 's real society .

249
00:23:51,055 --> 00:23:52,597
Oh .

250
00:23:52,848 --> 00:23:56,518
Sue , all I 've got is 50 cents . But you take it and buy yourself some dinner .

251
00:23:56,769 --> 00:23:58,770
- Oh , no , Cathy . - Come on .

252
00:23:59,021 --> 00:24:00,271
Mm-mm .

253
00:24:00,523 --> 00:24:03,066
My friend will give me some money tonight . Then I 'll stake you .

254
00:24:03,317 --> 00:24:04,734
I don 't need any mad money .

255
00:24:06,195 --> 00:24:07,237
I never get mad .

256
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:09,906
Good luck tonight at the Silver Slipper .

257
00:24:10,157 --> 00:24:11,616
- And don 't forget to duck . - Mm-mm !

258
00:24:26,715 --> 00:24:28,133
Toodle-loo .

259
00:24:54,952 --> 00:24:56,744
Just a moment , Miss Allen .

260
00:24:58,289 --> 00:25:01,916
- What are you coming in so quietly for ? - I didn 't want to disturb anybody .

261
00:25:02,168 --> 00:25:03,501
- Did you get the job ? - No .

262
00:25:03,752 --> 00:25:06,212
- Why not ? - I had trouble with the man who runs- -

263
00:25:06,463 --> 00:25:08,882
- Trouble ? - Mrs. Flannigan , you 'll get your money .

264
00:25:09,133 --> 00:25:10,800
Cathy promised to lend me some tonight

265
00:25:11,051 --> 00:25:11,718
when she comes home .

266
00:25:11,969 --> 00:25:15,263
You better get right up there , then . Because she 's home now .

267
00:25:15,931 --> 00:25:18,641
- Couldn 't it wait until tomorrow ? - No , it could not .

268
00:25:18,893 --> 00:25:22,604
If you want to sleep in this house tonight , you get that money .

269
00:25:24,023 --> 00:25:26,566
All right , I 'll try .

270
00:26:04,146 --> 00:26:05,688
Cathy .

271
00:26:09,026 --> 00:26:11,277
Cathy , it 's Sue . Are you there ?

272
00:26:14,406 --> 00:26:15,490
Cathy .

273
00:26:23,332 --> 00:26:24,040
Cathy ?

274
00:26:41,100 --> 00:26:42,934
I tell you , the scream came from up there .

275
00:26:48,107 --> 00:26:50,191
Let 's look into it .

276
00:27:43,454 --> 00:27:46,622
- Usually there 's a policeman at the corner . - That 's why I 'm blowing the whistle .

277
00:28:04,308 --> 00:28:07,143
Oh ! Cabbie ! Cabbie !

278
00:28:08,479 --> 00:28:11,522
Cabbie , cabbie !

279
00:30:34,124 --> 00:30:36,792
- Mrs. Andrews . - Sue .

280
00:30:40,255 --> 00:30:42,381
- What is it , Mother ? - It 's Sue .

281
00:30:42,633 --> 00:30:44,467
Sue . This is a surprise .

282
00:30:44,718 --> 00:30:46,552
I was just thinking about ... .

283
00:30:49,097 --> 00:30:51,307
- Sue ? - What happened to you , dear ?

284
00:30:51,558 --> 00:30:53,726
- What 's wrong ? - Wait a minute . Wait a minute .

285
00:30:53,977 --> 00:30:54,852
What happened , Sue ?

286
00:30:56,480 --> 00:30:57,813
What is it ?

287
00:30:58,065 --> 00:30:59,023
Cathy- -

288
00:30:59,274 --> 00:31:03,694
Cathy Gray , the girl in my rooming house , was murdered tonight .

289
00:31:03,946 --> 00:31:06,364
- What ? - I found her .

290
00:31:07,908 --> 00:31:10,660
The man who killed her was there in the room .

291
00:31:10,911 --> 00:31:13,454
I tried to get away from him .

292
00:31:16,166 --> 00:31:18,876
But he followed me into the street .

293
00:31:19,127 --> 00:31:22,046
No , Scott , no . Please don 't go out there .

294
00:31:22,339 --> 00:31:25,758
It 's all right , darling . Don 't be frightened .

295
00:31:26,176 --> 00:31:28,636
It 's all right now , dear . You 're safe .

296
00:31:43,610 --> 00:31:44,986
Who found the body ?

297
00:31:45,237 --> 00:31:47,863
One of my roomers . A friend of Cathy 's . Sue Allen .

298
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:49,657
Which one is Miss Allen ?

299
00:31:49,950 --> 00:31:52,118
- She isn 't here . - Where is she ?

300
00:31:52,494 --> 00:31:55,079
I don 't know . We heard her scream .

301
00:31:55,330 --> 00:31:57,498
When we went looking for her , she was gone .

302
00:31:57,749 --> 00:32:00,251
- Are all your roomers in ? - All but Miss Allen .

303
00:32:00,502 --> 00:32:01,627
Mm-hm .

304
00:32:01,878 --> 00:32:04,630
Lieutenant Brennan will want a statement from each one of you .

305
00:32:04,881 --> 00:32:06,382
See that nobody leaves the house .

306
00:32:14,266 --> 00:32:15,558
When I arrived at the rooming house

307
00:32:15,809 --> 00:32:18,436
this girl had been dead for several hours .

308
00:32:18,687 --> 00:32:21,147
The immediate cause of death was strangulation .

309
00:32:21,398 --> 00:32:23,983
The mark of a cord is still on her throat .

310
00:32:24,234 --> 00:32:27,320
My examination indicated she 'd probably been given a drug .

311
00:32:27,571 --> 00:32:29,905
- You were right . - What was it ?

312
00:32:30,157 --> 00:32:33,409
Something to make her sleep , Lieutenant Brennan . Veronal , perhaps .

313
00:32:33,660 --> 00:32:36,120
I 'll know as soon as we hear from the laboratory .

314
00:32:36,371 --> 00:32:38,372
How long would it take for such a drug to work ?

315
00:32:38,624 --> 00:32:40,875
That would depend upon how much it was diluted .

316
00:32:41,126 --> 00:32:43,628
Yes , it was probably given to her in a drink .

317
00:32:43,879 --> 00:32:45,963
That 's how it 's usually done .

318
00:32:47,049 --> 00:32:48,758
- Business is slow tonight . - What ?

319
00:32:49,009 --> 00:32:52,261
- Three suicides and two murders ... . - And a traffic case since 9 : 00 .

320
00:32:52,512 --> 00:32:54,639
The fellow got hit by an automobile .

321
00:32:54,890 --> 00:32:57,600
I didn 't think those things went fast enough to hurt anybody .

322
00:32:57,851 --> 00:32:58,851
Give them time .

323
00:32:59,102 --> 00:33:01,187
They 're getting better every day .

324
00:33:13,075 --> 00:33:16,160
I hope you like it here , honey . It 's the best we 've got .

325
00:33:25,379 --> 00:33:26,796
Hey , what 's the matter with this one ?

326
00:33:27,047 --> 00:33:28,464
You 'll get used to that .

327
00:33:28,715 --> 00:33:31,384
It 's the embalming fluid makes them jump .

328
00:33:31,635 --> 00:33:33,552
That 's one of the suicides . Just like a woman .

329
00:33:33,804 --> 00:33:36,305
They always have to have the last word .

330
00:36:00,575 --> 00:36:02,993
- Why didn 't you report this to the police ? - She 's doing that .

331
00:36:03,245 --> 00:36:04,537
Last night was the time to do it .

332
00:36:04,788 --> 00:36:08,123
- She was in no condition to come here . - This is murder , Mrs. Andrews .

333
00:36:10,335 --> 00:36:12,837
The body of Cathy Gray was stolen from the morgue last night .

334
00:36:13,088 --> 00:36:14,630
No .

335
00:36:14,881 --> 00:36:16,882
Why would anyone want to take Cathy 's body ?

336
00:36:17,133 --> 00:36:18,968
We 're as much in the dark as you are , Miss Allen .

337
00:36:19,928 --> 00:36:22,012
We had a similar case a few weeks back . Matthew Burke .

338
00:36:22,264 --> 00:36:22,972
I read about that .

339
00:36:23,223 --> 00:36:25,891
Yes , and Patterson , a deputy city attorney , disappeared .

340
00:36:26,142 --> 00:36:27,852
We found no trace of him .

341
00:36:29,354 --> 00:36:33,023
We could 've laid our hands on that man that you saw last night .

342
00:36:33,650 --> 00:36:36,610
You know , that 's the strangest description I 've ever heard .

343
00:36:37,279 --> 00:36:39,113
No human being can look like that .

344
00:36:39,364 --> 00:36:40,364
Sure you didn 't imagine it ?

345
00:36:40,615 --> 00:36:42,825
I did see him . Just as I described him to you .

346
00:36:43,076 --> 00:36:44,827
He was incredible , but very real .

347
00:36:45,078 --> 00:36:47,454
And he couldn 't be the same man who took Miss Gray to dinner ?

348
00:36:47,706 --> 00:36:48,831
That 's impossible .

349
00:36:49,082 --> 00:36:51,876
She told me before she went that he was very good-looking .

350
00:36:52,127 --> 00:36:53,919
That 's what the landlady said , it 's a man with gray hair .

351
00:36:54,921 --> 00:36:58,132
No use showing you any suspects , we have nothing that fits that description .

352
00:36:58,383 --> 00:37:00,217
If we did , we 'd have him in the crazy house .

353
00:37:00,468 --> 00:37:02,803
Don 't leave town . Where can we find you ?

354
00:37:03,054 --> 00:37:04,763
27 Lafayette Street .

355
00:37:05,015 --> 00:37:08,642
- Miss Allen will stay in our home . - Make sure of that . She 's our only witness .

356
00:37:08,894 --> 00:37:10,644
That 's all . Thank you .

357
00:37:39,674 --> 00:37:40,883
How do you do ?

358
00:37:41,134 --> 00:37:44,511
I received a letter giving this address and signed Professor Jarrod .

359
00:37:44,804 --> 00:37:48,807
But I know the professor 's dead . Can you tell me who wrote this letter ?

360
00:37:50,101 --> 00:37:52,144
My name is Sidney Wallace .

361
00:38:14,834 --> 00:38:17,211
- Mr. Wallace . - Professor .

362
00:38:17,462 --> 00:38:19,463
It 's so good- -

363
00:38:19,714 --> 00:38:23,467
Forgive me . Shaking hands with me is an unpleasant experience .

364
00:38:23,718 --> 00:38:27,304
My hands are no longer hands . Sit down , please .

365
00:38:27,555 --> 00:38:31,308
This is Igor . He 's a deaf-mute . He 's one of my assistants .

366
00:38:31,810 --> 00:38:36,105
I 'm going to open another wax museum under a different name .

367
00:38:36,356 --> 00:38:38,983
- It startled you , eh , seeing me here ? - That 's an understatement .

368
00:38:39,234 --> 00:38:42,403
- I thought you were dead . - Jarrod is dead . I am a reincarnation .

369
00:38:42,654 --> 00:38:45,572
When I saw your signature , I thought somebody was playing a joke on me .

370
00:38:45,824 --> 00:38:47,825
I still don 't understand how you escaped the fire .

371
00:38:48,076 --> 00:38:49,702
It 's a mystery to me , too , Mr. Wallace .

372
00:38:49,953 --> 00:38:52,663
All I can remember is that I tried to get out of my studio .

373
00:38:52,914 --> 00:38:56,250
- I failed at first , but here I am . - What a frightful experience .

374
00:38:56,501 --> 00:38:59,253
Somehow I made my way to the house of a doctor .

375
00:38:59,504 --> 00:39:02,881
I still have my limbs , though they won 't bear the weight of my body .

376
00:39:03,633 --> 00:39:06,969
As for my hands , they are no use to me now .

377
00:39:07,220 --> 00:39:11,098
As a sculptor , I can 't control them . But they serve for ordinary functions .

378
00:39:11,641 --> 00:39:12,891
But you 're beginning again ?

379
00:39:13,143 --> 00:39:15,436
With the help of my pupils , yes .

380
00:39:15,687 --> 00:39:18,689
I 'm rebuilding my exhibition from the ground up .

381
00:39:18,940 --> 00:39:21,025
I 'm going to give the people what they want :

382
00:39:21,276 --> 00:39:23,360
Sensation , horror , shock .

383
00:39:23,611 --> 00:39:26,155
Send them out in the streets to tell their friends

384
00:39:26,406 --> 00:39:28,866
how wonderful it is to be scared to death .

385
00:39:29,868 --> 00:39:32,036
I 'll show you one of my subjects .

386
00:39:32,954 --> 00:39:36,999
Do you recall the case of Kemmler , the first man to die in the electric chair ?

387
00:39:37,250 --> 00:39:41,420
- Yes . - Igor is working on a model of his head .

388
00:39:41,963 --> 00:39:44,798
He has a strange obsession , this mute of mine .

389
00:39:45,050 --> 00:39:48,844
Every head he models takes on the shape of his own face .

390
00:39:49,095 --> 00:39:53,515
But in this case I humor him , for actually he somewhat resembles Kemmler .

391
00:39:53,767 --> 00:39:55,017
Uh ... .

392
00:39:55,477 --> 00:39:58,437
Crimes of violence will be reproduced in wax

393
00:39:58,688 --> 00:40:01,899
and exhibited while they are still fresh in the public mind .

394
00:40:02,150 --> 00:40:04,109
What do you think of my scheme ?

395
00:40:04,944 --> 00:40:06,695
I think it will succeed , commercially

396
00:40:06,946 --> 00:40:08,864
though it doesn 't sound like you .

397
00:40:09,157 --> 00:40:10,866
Have you turned your back on beauty ?

398
00:40:11,117 --> 00:40:12,159
No .

399
00:40:13,078 --> 00:40:15,162
No , but I can no longer create it .

400
00:40:15,497 --> 00:40:17,498
I never forgot your Marie Antoinette .

401
00:40:17,749 --> 00:40:19,166
Nor have I.

402
00:40:19,667 --> 00:40:22,169
She will be the leading lady of my new exhibition .

403
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:24,922
- But I must find her first . - Find her ?

404
00:40:25,173 --> 00:40:26,715
A model , I mean .

405
00:40:26,966 --> 00:40:30,636
Yes , there will be beauty , for contrast , if nothing else .

406
00:40:30,887 --> 00:40:33,639
But each subject must be taken from life .

407
00:40:33,890 --> 00:40:37,935
How can I convince my audience they 're alive , if I don 't believe it myself ?

408
00:40:38,186 --> 00:40:40,687
Oh , I have something I think will interest you .

409
00:40:43,441 --> 00:40:46,360
You follow Igor down into the basement .

410
00:40:47,904 --> 00:40:49,863
I have to go my own way .

411
00:41:08,299 --> 00:41:11,301
Here we are . Interesting , isn 't it ?

412
00:41:11,553 --> 00:41:14,930
One of my pupils is about to dip a body into a bath of wax .

413
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:16,348
- Body ? - Yes .

414
00:41:16,599 --> 00:41:18,517
The bodies are constructed separately

415
00:41:18,768 --> 00:41:22,271
to exact specifications , of reinforced plaster of Paris .

416
00:41:22,522 --> 00:41:25,440
Oh , uh , this is Leon , another one of my pupils .

417
00:41:25,692 --> 00:41:27,359
- Mr. Wallace . - How do you do ?

418
00:41:27,610 --> 00:41:31,196
The wax is melted in the caldron you see above the vat

419
00:41:31,447 --> 00:41:33,824
liquefied and brought to a boiling point

420
00:41:34,075 --> 00:41:37,452
so that it will distribute itself evenly over the body .

421
00:41:37,704 --> 00:41:40,455
The head and hands , tinted by my own secret process

422
00:41:40,707 --> 00:41:44,042
are attached to the body after it is covered with its skin of wax .

423
00:41:44,294 --> 00:41:45,836
Now watch .

424
00:42:18,411 --> 00:42:19,870
I often wondered how that was done .

425
00:42:20,121 --> 00:42:22,915
It 's a method of my own . Crude but adequate .

426
00:42:27,003 --> 00:42:31,089
- Have you found a home for your museum ? - This is it . The building upstairs , I mean .

427
00:42:31,341 --> 00:42:34,843
We 'll continue to use the cellar as a workshop . Cut a door here and there .

428
00:42:35,094 --> 00:42:38,805
But it 's an excellent location , and the building can be leased at the right price .

429
00:42:39,057 --> 00:42:42,893
I have some capital , but I need more . Thirty thousand , at least .

430
00:42:43,144 --> 00:42:45,312
That 's why I 've asked you to come here .

431
00:42:45,939 --> 00:42:48,190
- I 'll think it over . - Good .

432
00:42:48,441 --> 00:42:49,608
She 's about right , now .

433
00:42:49,859 --> 00:42:52,986
Leon , drain out the surplus , and let her cool .

434
00:42:54,656 --> 00:42:56,698
Oh , Leon , open up Number 27 .

435
00:42:57,158 --> 00:42:58,867
Come this way , please .

436
00:42:59,744 --> 00:43:03,080
I told you that I intend to exhibit scenes of violence .

437
00:43:03,331 --> 00:43:05,290
Here is an interesting subject .

438
00:43:05,541 --> 00:43:07,793
A mystery they 're still talking about .

439
00:43:08,253 --> 00:43:09,461
All right , Leon .

440
00:43:11,589 --> 00:43:14,508
I saw that man 's picture in the papers . This is a remarkable likeness .

441
00:43:14,759 --> 00:43:17,844
- But it can 't be a death mask . - No , it 's from memory .

442
00:43:23,434 --> 00:43:25,936
He hanged himself in an elevator shaft .

443
00:43:47,750 --> 00:43:51,003
Come in , ladies and gentlemen . See the House of Wax .

444
00:43:54,674 --> 00:43:56,091
See the Chamber of Horrors .

445
00:44:01,306 --> 00:44:03,724
Here 's three lovely ladies right over here .

446
00:44:05,685 --> 00:44:07,227
Would you like to see Little Egypt ?

447
00:44:07,478 --> 00:44:08,562
Here she is , ladies and gentlemen

448
00:44:08,813 --> 00:44:10,856
Little Egypt , queen of the harem

449
00:44:11,107 --> 00:44:14,860
who danced at the Colombian Exposition in Chicago in 1893 .

450
00:44:15,111 --> 00:44:17,988
Is she wax , or is she flesh and blood ?

451
00:44:18,239 --> 00:44:21,033
See the world in wax , the Hall of Fame .

452
00:44:21,284 --> 00:44:22,200
The Chamber of Horrors .

453
00:44:22,452 --> 00:44:25,704
A cultural exhibition that 'll enlighten you , amaze you ... .

454
00:44:25,955 --> 00:44:28,415
- I think I could do that . - Oh , you couldn 't .

455
00:44:28,666 --> 00:44:30,917
I could , too , if I took my stays off .

456
00:44:31,461 --> 00:44:33,086
Don 't do that . Don 't talk that way .

457
00:44:33,338 --> 00:44:34,004
Watch it , young lady .

458
00:44:35,923 --> 00:44:36,715
Careful , sir .

459
00:44:36,966 --> 00:44:38,925
Keep your head down or I 'll tap you on the chin .

460
00:44:39,177 --> 00:44:40,177
Look out . Duck !

461
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:44,514
Wow , that 's a becoming hat you 're wearing .

462
00:44:44,766 --> 00:44:46,892
I wonder if I could clip a flower off it .

463
00:44:47,143 --> 00:44:48,769
Hold steady . Don 't move your head .

464
00:44:49,020 --> 00:44:51,438
Or you 'll lose the powder off your nose .

465
00:44:52,440 --> 00:44:54,566
There is someone with a bag of popcorn .

466
00:44:54,817 --> 00:44:55,776
Close your mouth .

467
00:44:56,027 --> 00:44:58,278
It 's the bag I 'm aiming at , not your tonsil .

468
00:44:58,529 --> 00:44:59,696
Here she comes .

469
00:44:59,947 --> 00:45:01,406
Well , look at that , it 's in the bag .

470
00:45:02,033 --> 00:45:05,285
See the lovely centers of ancient times .

471
00:45:05,536 --> 00:45:08,288
Beauties who died in torture a nd on the block .

472
00:45:08,539 --> 00:45:10,040
Visit our Chamber of Horrors

473
00:45:10,291 --> 00:45:12,751
and pass the time with notorious murderers

474
00:45:13,002 --> 00:45:16,046
who killed with the rope , the knife , and the ax .

475
00:45:16,464 --> 00:45:21,259
Thrills , chills , and laughter for a price within the reach of all .

476
00:45:21,511 --> 00:45:24,930
I hope you don 't think I 've gone too far hiring this fellow to bring people in .

477
00:45:25,181 --> 00:45:28,058
- He makes it sound like a sideshow . - Try him for a week or two .

478
00:45:28,309 --> 00:45:30,477
Once we 're established , we won 't need that sort of thing .

479
00:45:40,363 --> 00:45:41,822
He looks like a real man .

480
00:45:42,073 --> 00:45:43,448
You 'd be surprised .

481
00:45:43,699 --> 00:45:45,617
It is a real man . Sorry .

482
00:45:46,369 --> 00:45:49,830
The historic figures I 'm about to show you will be more interesting

483
00:45:50,081 --> 00:45:53,959
when I tell you that their faces were molded from the original death masks

484
00:45:54,210 --> 00:45:57,129
now in the possession of certain European governments .

485
00:45:57,380 --> 00:45:59,089
First , we have Anne Boleyn

486
00:45:59,340 --> 00:46:02,467
second wife of Henry the VIII , and the mother of Queen Elizabeth

487
00:46:02,718 --> 00:46:05,512
with the executioner Henry borrowed from the French king

488
00:46:05,763 --> 00:46:09,683
so that Anne 's head would be cleaved from her body without too much pain .

489
00:46:09,934 --> 00:46:11,893
He was a thoughtful husband , Henry .

490
00:46:12,145 --> 00:46:14,771
It was he who invented the short cut to divorce .

491
00:46:15,356 --> 00:46:17,691
A very bad pun , I 'm afraid .

492
00:46:17,942 --> 00:46:20,527
Here is another scene of historic violence .

493
00:46:20,778 --> 00:46:22,529
Charlotte Corday and Marat

494
00:46:22,780 --> 00:46:24,614
one of the leaders of the French Revolution .

495
00:46:24,866 --> 00:46:27,075
The lady found him taking a bath

496
00:46:27,326 --> 00:46:29,119
and plunged the knife into his heart .

497
00:46:30,455 --> 00:46:31,621
What a shocking thing .

498
00:46:31,873 --> 00:46:35,500
Yes , wasn 't it ? The poor man was dreadfully embarrassed .

499
00:46:38,629 --> 00:46:40,797
The exhibits in this room will be added to

500
00:46:41,048 --> 00:46:43,550
from time to time as various crimes are committed .

501
00:46:43,801 --> 00:46:46,052
You will read about them in your newspaper

502
00:46:46,304 --> 00:46:49,264
and see them enacted here in waxen tableaux .

503
00:46:49,515 --> 00:46:50,515
Oh , by the way , ladies

504
00:46:50,766 --> 00:46:54,936
this is how your ancestor carried his bride across the threshold .

505
00:46:55,188 --> 00:46:56,480
During the French Revolution

506
00:46:56,731 --> 00:46:59,608
a certain doctor invented a labor-saving device

507
00:46:59,859 --> 00:47:01,902
to take the place of a headmen 's ax .

508
00:47:02,153 --> 00:47:04,279
So successful was this machine

509
00:47:04,530 --> 00:47:06,990
at cutting off the heads of the French aristocrats

510
00:47:07,241 --> 00:47:08,867
they named it after its creator .

511
00:47:09,118 --> 00:47:11,328
And here it is , the bloody guillotine .

512
00:47:15,166 --> 00:47:17,250
Oh , dear , I don 't think I can stand it .

513
00:47:17,502 --> 00:47:19,127
Now , Millie , pull yourself together , honey .

514
00:47:19,378 --> 00:47:20,212
Twelve years ago

515
00:47:20,463 --> 00:47:23,590
the electric chair was first used in New York state .

516
00:47:23,841 --> 00:47:25,675
Here we have an authentic reproduction

517
00:47:25,927 --> 00:47:30,597
of the execution of William Kemmler on August 3rd in 1890 .

518
00:47:30,848 --> 00:47:32,682
Kemmler killed without mercy

519
00:47:32,934 --> 00:47:36,186
and 2000 volts sent him to a higher court .

520
00:47:36,521 --> 00:47:39,314
The torture of the rack . In this case

521
00:47:39,565 --> 00:47:44,027
Lady Anne Askew , an English noblewoman accused of treason

522
00:47:44,278 --> 00:47:45,695
is being put to the question .

523
00:47:45,947 --> 00:47:48,657
Needless to say , she admitted she was a traitor .

524
00:47:48,908 --> 00:47:50,825
Who wouldn 't , under that sort of pressure ?

525
00:47:51,077 --> 00:47:52,494
- Oh , dear . - Is it your corset ?

526
00:47:52,745 --> 00:47:54,412
No , it 's my stomach . It turned over .

527
00:47:54,664 --> 00:47:55,789
Mine turned over too .

528
00:47:56,040 --> 00:47:56,748
And now , my friends

529
00:47:57,250 --> 00:48:01,920
we have that jolly old gentleman known as the modern Bluebeard .

530
00:48:02,171 --> 00:48:06,383
Like his namesake , he killed not wisely , but too well

531
00:48:06,717 --> 00:48:09,302
and did away with eight wives .

532
00:48:11,097 --> 00:48:12,973
Oh , Millie !

533
00:48:13,224 --> 00:48:15,559
Smelling salts , ladies ? Help yourself .

534
00:48:15,810 --> 00:48:17,310
Thank you very much .

535
00:48:19,146 --> 00:48:22,315
Next door to him , we have a mystery of more recent date .

536
00:48:22,567 --> 00:48:24,776
Matthew Burke , the stockbroker .

537
00:48:25,027 --> 00:48:29,823
He was found hanged in the elevator shaft of the building where he had his offices .

538
00:48:31,117 --> 00:48:33,994
Was it murder or suicide ?

539
00:48:34,245 --> 00:48:36,621
Only time will tell .

540
00:48:36,872 --> 00:48:42,210
" Foul deeds will rise , though all the world overwhelm them , to men 's eyes . "

541
00:48:50,136 --> 00:48:52,220
Oh , heh . Thank you .

542
00:48:52,471 --> 00:48:54,973
- You like him , Sue ? - He looks like my Uncle Rufus .

543
00:48:55,224 --> 00:48:57,726
They ought to have a policeman like this in the Eden Musée .

544
00:48:57,977 --> 00:48:59,853
- Haven 't you been there ? - No .

545
00:49:00,104 --> 00:49:02,897
From what I see in the papers , this museum is even better .

546
00:49:03,149 --> 00:49:04,649
Anyway , we 'll soon find out .

547
00:49:04,900 --> 00:49:06,192
Scott .

548
00:49:06,861 --> 00:49:08,320
Mr. Wallace .

549
00:49:09,030 --> 00:49:11,448
Sue , I want you to meet my good friend , Mr. Sidney Wallace .

550
00:49:11,699 --> 00:49:13,116
- Miss Sue Allen . - It 's a pleasure .

551
00:49:13,367 --> 00:49:15,660
- I heard you were in town . - You should have looked me up .

552
00:49:15,911 --> 00:49:19,372
I expect great things of Scott . I consider him one of our most promising sculptors .

553
00:49:19,749 --> 00:49:21,958
- Has he been working hard ? - He never knows when to stop .

554
00:49:22,209 --> 00:49:24,586
- Sue 's been posing for me . - Indeed , lovely subject .

555
00:49:24,837 --> 00:49:26,880
- Thank you . - Not a professional model . She 's a guest .

556
00:49:27,131 --> 00:49:28,715
Sue 's mother and mine were great friends .

557
00:49:28,966 --> 00:49:30,008
- Have you been inside ? - Yes .

558
00:49:30,259 --> 00:49:31,009
Is it exciting ?

559
00:49:31,260 --> 00:49:32,510
If anything , too much so .

560
00:49:32,762 --> 00:49:33,928
But I 'm sure it 'll catch on .

561
00:49:34,180 --> 00:49:36,139
Jarrod , the man who owns the place , is a good friend .

562
00:49:36,390 --> 00:49:38,433
You 'll be interested in him , Scott . Let 's go in , shall we ?

563
00:49:47,526 --> 00:49:50,820
- You know , these figures are excellent . - I thought you 'd agree with me .

564
00:49:51,072 --> 00:49:53,657
They 're not only well done but they 're good theater .

565
00:49:53,908 --> 00:49:56,242
- What do you think , Miss Allen ? - I know they are only wax

566
00:49:56,494 --> 00:49:59,496
but they seem so real , just looking at her makes my neck hurt .

567
00:49:59,747 --> 00:50:01,790
Wait till you see the Chamber of Horrors .

568
00:50:02,041 --> 00:50:04,751
I told Jarrod he should have a nurse on duty there .

569
00:50:05,961 --> 00:50:08,421
- You know that he lost the use of his hands . - Oh ?

570
00:50:08,673 --> 00:50:11,549
- Who did these figures ? - His pupils , but he supervised the work .

571
00:50:11,801 --> 00:50:14,219
- His is the mastermind . - Surely knows his anatomy .

572
00:51:10,901 --> 00:51:11,693
Sue , what is it ?

573
00:51:13,863 --> 00:51:16,698
- Sue , are you crying ? - What 's wrong , Miss Allen ?

574
00:51:16,949 --> 00:51:19,659
A dear friend of mine was murdered and I found her .

575
00:51:19,910 --> 00:51:23,329
She means Cathy Gray , the girl whose body was stolen from the morgue .

576
00:51:23,581 --> 00:51:25,540
What made you think of her now ?

577
00:51:25,916 --> 00:51:26,750
That 's her face .

578
00:51:27,001 --> 00:51:29,878
That 's Cathy 's face , Scott . I know every line of it .

579
00:51:30,129 --> 00:51:33,006
I wake up at night and I see it . I can 't get it out of my mind .

580
00:51:33,257 --> 00:51:35,633
Perhaps that 's the reason you see a resemblance in this figure .

581
00:51:35,885 --> 00:51:38,386
- It 's more than a resemblance . - It 's wax , my dear .

582
00:51:38,637 --> 00:51:40,805
I know , I know , but ... .

583
00:51:41,182 --> 00:51:43,558
Why should it be so like Cathy ?

584
00:51:43,809 --> 00:51:45,351
I think I can explain that .

585
00:51:46,437 --> 00:51:47,103
Oh , uh

586
00:51:47,354 --> 00:51:49,773
Miss Allen , Scott Andrews , Mr. Henry Jarrod .

587
00:51:50,024 --> 00:51:51,983
- This is a pleasure . - You see , Miss Allen- -

588
00:51:52,234 --> 00:51:54,486
Yes , I heard what the young lady said .

589
00:51:54,737 --> 00:51:58,239
The figure of Joan of Arc is a traditional exhibit in wax museums .

590
00:51:58,491 --> 00:52:01,117
It was completed just in time for our opening tonight .

591
00:52:01,368 --> 00:52:04,913
You 're right , my dear . It is more than a chance resemblance .

592
00:52:05,164 --> 00:52:08,625
When I create an important figure , I can 't take just any face .

593
00:52:08,876 --> 00:52:11,586
I saw pictures of your Cathy Gray in the newspaper .

594
00:52:11,837 --> 00:52:15,048
Her face fascinated me . And , well , here she is .

595
00:52:15,299 --> 00:52:18,092
Immortalized as the victim of an earlier event .

596
00:52:18,761 --> 00:52:23,181
- Do you really think she 'd mind ? - No , I don 't think she 'd mind .

597
00:52:23,432 --> 00:52:27,727
Cathy loved to " dress up " as she called it . She used to take fancy dresses

598
00:52:27,978 --> 00:52:30,146
and imitate the actresses she saw in the theater .

599
00:52:30,898 --> 00:52:33,399
- I don 't think she 'd mind . - Then I 'm forgiven ?

600
00:52:33,651 --> 00:52:35,944
Well , there 's nothing to forgive .

601
00:52:36,362 --> 00:52:39,030
I just don 't understand how it can seem so real .

602
00:52:39,281 --> 00:52:43,117
That 's the finest compliment I 've ever received . Thank you , my dear .

603
00:52:43,369 --> 00:52:45,495
Did I hear your name correctly , Scott Andrews ?

604
00:52:45,746 --> 00:52:48,373
- Yes , Mr. Jarrod . - The sculptor I 've been telling you about .

605
00:52:48,624 --> 00:52:51,334
Oh , Sidney showed me some photographs of your work .

606
00:52:51,585 --> 00:52:53,211
He was right . You have great promise .

607
00:52:53,462 --> 00:52:56,506
- What are you doing now ? - I 'm doing a head of Miss Allen .

608
00:52:56,757 --> 00:52:58,466
Let me see your hands .

609
00:52:59,510 --> 00:53:00,969
Yes .

610
00:53:01,679 --> 00:53:03,847
Yes , mine were once like that .

611
00:53:05,850 --> 00:53:07,517
How I envy you .

612
00:53:07,768 --> 00:53:08,726
Mr. Andrews .

613
00:53:08,978 --> 00:53:12,897
Would you be interested in some modeling for me , some originals I have in mind ?

614
00:53:13,148 --> 00:53:14,315
Why , yes . I 'd be honored .

615
00:53:14,567 --> 00:53:17,652
Good . Come here tomorrow morning , we 'll make the arrangements .

616
00:53:17,903 --> 00:53:19,654
I think you 'll like it .

617
00:53:19,905 --> 00:53:20,738
Sidney .

618
00:53:21,782 --> 00:53:24,242
- I want you to look at this girl . - With pleasure .

619
00:53:24,493 --> 00:53:26,119
Who does she remind you of ?

620
00:53:26,370 --> 00:53:28,204
I 've been wondering about that .

621
00:53:28,455 --> 00:53:30,373
I haven 't known Miss Allen more than 10 minutes

622
00:53:30,624 --> 00:53:32,250
but there 's something about her face- -

623
00:53:32,501 --> 00:53:35,670
That haunts you as the face of my Marie Antoinette has haunted me .

624
00:53:35,921 --> 00:53:37,589
Marie Antoinette ?

625
00:53:37,840 --> 00:53:40,425
Of course . I should have seen it at once .

626
00:53:40,676 --> 00:53:42,844
A figure in wax . Mr. Jarrod 's greatest work .

627
00:53:43,095 --> 00:53:45,430
More than wax . She lived .

628
00:53:45,681 --> 00:53:48,933
- You mean I look like she did ? - Exactly as she did .

629
00:53:49,184 --> 00:53:52,520
Once in his lifetime , every artist feels the hand of God

630
00:53:52,771 --> 00:53:55,189
and creates something that comes alive .

631
00:53:55,733 --> 00:53:58,818
So it was with my Marie Antoinette . And I loved her .

632
00:53:59,486 --> 00:54:03,615
But she 's gone now . Horribly destroyed .

633
00:54:04,909 --> 00:54:06,910
Perhaps you will help me to bring her back .

634
00:54:07,995 --> 00:54:10,955
You will come to see me again soon ?

635
00:54:11,206 --> 00:54:12,248
I 'd be glad to .

636
00:54:13,459 --> 00:54:16,711
You 'll be welcome at any time , no matter what I 'm doing .

637
00:54:16,962 --> 00:54:18,504
And you , Mr. Andrews , in the morning ?

638
00:54:18,756 --> 00:54:21,424
- I 'll be here , very eager to begin . - Thank you .

639
00:54:21,675 --> 00:54:24,552
It 's been a very exciting day for me and I 'm a little tired .

640
00:54:24,803 --> 00:54:27,805
So if you 'll forgive me , I 'll say good night .

641
00:54:30,142 --> 00:54:33,019
- Oh , uh , Sidney , one moment , please . - Excuse me .

642
00:54:33,270 --> 00:54:34,479
I 'll be right back .

643
00:54:35,814 --> 00:54:38,149
Forget about it , Sue . You heard what Mr. Jarrod said .

644
00:54:38,400 --> 00:54:41,444
Cathy 's face was inspiration . It 's a portrait in wax .

645
00:54:41,695 --> 00:54:43,947
Why should it seem so real ?

646
00:54:49,745 --> 00:54:51,496
I hate to drag you away , Scott .

647
00:54:51,747 --> 00:54:54,958
Oh , that 's all right . I 'm gonna work here . We 'll see it all another time .

648
00:54:55,209 --> 00:54:56,918
Yes , another time .

649
00:54:57,294 --> 00:55:00,380
Still time to see the entire exhibition .

650
00:55:00,631 --> 00:55:02,757
Get your tickets from the charming lady

651
00:55:03,008 --> 00:55:04,592
in the box office and go right in .

652
00:55:04,843 --> 00:55:07,053
See the world in wax and improve your mind .

653
00:55:07,304 --> 00:55:08,888
See the Chamber of Horrors

654
00:55:09,139 --> 00:55:11,432
and scare yourself out of a year 's growth .

655
00:55:27,741 --> 00:55:28,908
Not again .

656
00:57:04,338 --> 00:57:06,172
What happened , Sue ? Why did you scream ?

657
00:57:06,423 --> 00:57:07,757
I saw Cathy again .

658
00:57:08,008 --> 00:57:10,343
And the man who killed her was right in this room .

659
00:57:12,137 --> 00:57:14,138
I must have been dreaming .

660
00:57:14,389 --> 00:57:16,766
Of course you were , dear .

661
00:58:15,784 --> 00:58:17,493
A lager for the gentleman .

662
00:58:17,953 --> 00:58:19,453
Sarsaparilla for the lady .

663
00:58:20,289 --> 00:58:23,666
- And two knockwurst on rye . - Thank you .

664
00:58:25,919 --> 00:58:28,754
- Enjoying yourself ? - It 's exciting .

665
00:58:29,006 --> 00:58:31,799
- Do nice people come here ? - Ha , ha . Of course .

666
00:58:32,050 --> 00:58:34,760
- These Sunday matinees are very popular . - I don 't know .

667
00:58:35,012 --> 00:58:38,472
It doesn 't seem proper , all those girls showing their ... .

668
00:58:38,724 --> 00:58:40,558
- Their talents . - Heh .

669
00:58:40,809 --> 00:58:42,977
You never saw a show like this in Provincetown ?

670
00:58:43,228 --> 00:58:45,855
- No . - Heh . Don 't worry , your reputation is safe .

671
00:58:46,106 --> 00:58:48,316
You 've been going around with the weight of the world on your shoulders .

672
00:58:48,567 --> 00:58:51,694
Worrying about wax figures and seeing monsters in your dreams .

673
00:58:51,945 --> 00:58:55,406
You need something like this to bring you back to normalcy .

674
00:58:55,657 --> 00:58:57,116
Sue .

675
00:59:27,522 --> 00:59:29,398
- Scott . - Hmm ?

676
00:59:29,733 --> 00:59:33,194
Remember Mr. Jarrod said he first saw Cathy 's picture in the newspaper ?

677
00:59:33,487 --> 00:59:35,696
Yes . What 's wrong with that ?

678
00:59:36,281 --> 00:59:37,949
I knew her so well .

679
00:59:39,284 --> 00:59:41,744
I knew every little expression and they 're all there .

680
00:59:41,995 --> 00:59:43,829
Well , they would be . The man 's an artist .

681
00:59:44,706 --> 00:59:48,084
There 's something else I saw that night in the museum .

682
00:59:48,335 --> 00:59:51,754
Cathy had a habit of wearing an earring in her right ear .

683
00:59:52,005 --> 00:59:55,841
She had the lobe of her right ear only pierced for that .

684
00:59:56,510 --> 00:59:57,927
Well , that 's there too .

685
00:59:58,512 --> 01:00:00,429
How could he see that in a photograph ?

686
01:00:01,181 --> 01:00:04,433
- How can he make it so real unless ... . - What ?

687
01:00:06,478 --> 01:00:07,770
Unless it is Cathy .

688
01:00:08,605 --> 01:00:12,525
Sue . Now , look , I 'm gonna take you to Lieutenant Brennan 's office tomorrow .

689
01:00:12,776 --> 01:00:15,069
I want you to tell him exactly what you 've told me here now .

690
01:00:15,320 --> 01:00:16,445
He 's a policeman , he knows .

691
01:00:16,697 --> 01:00:19,865
He 'll convince you once and for all that no such thing could happen .

692
01:00:20,117 --> 01:00:22,868
Now , relax , honey , and enjoy the show .

693
01:00:56,403 --> 01:01:00,114
I know it sounds fantastic , but you asked me to tell you everything .

694
01:01:00,365 --> 01:01:04,076
You can see this idea 's become an obsession , an unhealthy one , if you ask me .

695
01:01:04,328 --> 01:01:07,288
- You say Jarrod 's a cripple ? - He uses a wheelchair .

696
01:01:07,539 --> 01:01:10,249
He can walk with crutches , but , uh , not very well .

697
01:01:10,500 --> 01:01:13,878
Such a man came and asked to see police photographs of Cathy Gray .

698
01:01:14,129 --> 01:01:18,007
You see , that 's how it 's done . Every detail is studied to make the features true to life .

699
01:01:18,258 --> 01:01:20,718
But why should Joan of Arc have her right ear pierced ?

700
01:01:20,969 --> 01:01:23,554
- Why not ? They wore them then . - Two , not one .

701
01:01:24,181 --> 01:01:28,142
I don 't know , lieutenant , it 's not a suspicion . It 's more a kind of fear , an intuition .

702
01:01:28,393 --> 01:01:32,021
Well , intuition isn 't much help in police work . Facts are what we need .

703
01:01:32,272 --> 01:01:35,483
Suppose you forget about it , and let us do the worrying , eh ?

704
01:01:35,734 --> 01:01:37,485
You mean you 'll investigate it ?

705
01:01:37,736 --> 01:01:39,695
- Of course he does . - Yes , that 's what I mean .

706
01:01:39,946 --> 01:01:43,074
- You both think I 'm crazy . - Oh , we think nothing of the kind .

707
01:01:43,325 --> 01:01:46,952
It was very good of you to listen and be so patient . Thank you .

708
01:01:47,329 --> 01:01:48,871
- Goodbye . - Goodbye .

709
01:01:49,122 --> 01:01:50,498
Thanks .

710
01:01:56,671 --> 01:01:59,090
This is Brennan speaking . Give me Shane .

711
01:01:59,800 --> 01:02:02,301
Hello , Jim . I want you to go to the City License Bureau

712
01:02:02,552 --> 01:02:04,887
and check up on a man named Henry Jarrod .

713
01:02:05,138 --> 01:02:09,058
Yes , he opened a museum on 29th Street , near Broadway .

714
01:02:10,018 --> 01:02:11,811
Yes , The House of Wax .

715
01:02:12,062 --> 01:02:15,648
Dig up all you can . Get a list of his employees and check with me here .

716
01:02:15,899 --> 01:02:17,441
Right .

717
01:02:41,925 --> 01:02:43,634
That 's a copy of her face , all right .

718
01:02:43,885 --> 01:02:46,470
She didn 't look like that the night we saw her in the rooming house .

719
01:02:46,721 --> 01:02:49,265
- Not so composed . - No . Poor kid .

720
01:02:49,516 --> 01:02:51,142
Hey , you know , this fellow Jarrod 's good .

721
01:02:51,393 --> 01:02:53,227
You don 't think Miss Allen 's fears are justified ?

722
01:02:53,478 --> 01:02:55,020
Why , heck , no . Do you ?

723
01:02:55,272 --> 01:02:57,606
That 's wax , how could it be anything else ?

724
01:02:57,858 --> 01:03:00,943
Leave it to a skirt to dream up a crazy idea like that .

725
01:03:40,984 --> 01:03:43,694
So you did come to see me , my Marie Antoinette ?

726
01:03:43,945 --> 01:03:45,821
Or was it that you came to see ?

727
01:03:46,072 --> 01:03:48,157
Mr. Jarrod , I 'm so sorry .

728
01:03:48,408 --> 01:03:50,242
I know I 'm not supposed to touch the figures .

729
01:03:50,494 --> 01:03:52,828
But you couldn 't help yourself . Don 't let it trouble you .

730
01:03:53,079 --> 01:03:55,915
Oh , I beg your pardon , this is Leon Averill and Igor .

731
01:03:56,166 --> 01:03:57,166
How do you do ?

732
01:03:57,417 --> 01:04:00,169
Igor isn 't impolite . He simply can 't talk .

733
01:04:00,420 --> 01:04:02,129
Leon is an artist in his own right .

734
01:04:02,380 --> 01:04:05,424
It was he who did the waxwork on the figure of Joan of Arc .

735
01:04:05,675 --> 01:04:09,261
- Does she still seem real to you ? - As life itself .

736
01:04:09,513 --> 01:04:12,473
Of course , her hair is different , but that doesn 't change her face .

737
01:04:13,517 --> 01:04:17,686
What puzzles me is how you can get such detail from a photo .

738
01:04:19,022 --> 01:04:22,149
Was Cathy wearing her earrings when the police photographed her ?

739
01:04:22,400 --> 01:04:25,361
Earrings ? I don 't remember . Was she , Leon ?

740
01:04:26,613 --> 01:04:28,781
No . No . I don 't think so .

741
01:04:29,032 --> 01:04:31,825
The police would remove the jewelry from the body , wouldn 't they ?

742
01:04:32,077 --> 01:04:35,454
Yet you were careful to show that both her ears had been pierced for them .

743
01:04:35,705 --> 01:04:37,831
Ha-ha-ha . Yes , of course .

744
01:04:38,083 --> 01:04:41,710
If I missed a detail of that sort , Mr. Jarrod would be most displeased .

745
01:04:41,962 --> 01:04:44,129
He insists on reality .

746
01:04:44,381 --> 01:04:45,673
I can understand that .

747
01:04:45,924 --> 01:04:47,508
Oh , just a moment , Leon .

748
01:04:47,759 --> 01:04:51,387
There 's something in this box I think would interest you . Open it , Leon .

749
01:04:57,936 --> 01:05:01,730
Your Mr. Andrews permitted us to make a cast of the head he did of you .

750
01:05:02,190 --> 01:05:05,442
Leon has just finished it in wax . Do you like it ?

751
01:05:06,111 --> 01:05:09,738
It 's sort of a shock to see your head detached that way .

752
01:05:10,240 --> 01:05:11,949
I guess it 's a very good likeness .

753
01:05:12,200 --> 01:05:13,492
Yes , and no .

754
01:05:13,743 --> 01:05:16,495
Andrews is clever , but like all modern sculptors

755
01:05:16,746 --> 01:05:19,957
he has too much imagination . He would improve on nature .

756
01:05:20,208 --> 01:05:22,918
What I need for my Marie Antoinette is you .

757
01:05:23,169 --> 01:05:24,670
The real you .

758
01:05:24,921 --> 01:05:26,547
Nothing less will satisfy me .

759
01:05:27,507 --> 01:05:30,593
Will you come to see me again , my dear ?

760
01:05:53,491 --> 01:05:55,576
Hey , Burke .

761
01:05:55,827 --> 01:05:59,038
You know this fellow Jarrod 's quicker at finding these guys than we are ?

762
01:05:59,289 --> 01:06:01,999
That 's what he says in his advertising .

763
01:06:02,250 --> 01:06:04,918
Look at that . Even the twist in the neck .

764
01:06:05,170 --> 01:06:07,671
That 's a case that gets me . Where is Burke ? Who got him ?

765
01:06:07,922 --> 01:06:10,716
- Who 'd want him ? - We better find out pretty quick .

766
01:06:10,967 --> 01:06:13,802
- You read the blast in this morning 's World ? - Yeah , it 's dynamite .

767
01:06:14,054 --> 01:06:16,138
Chief had me in his office this morning .

768
01:06:16,389 --> 01:06:18,932
If I 'm not careful , I 'll be pounding a beat in the Bronx .

769
01:06:29,986 --> 01:06:31,487
Come here , Jim .

770
01:06:34,074 --> 01:06:37,284
You remember Wilbur Patterson , the deputy city attorney who disappeared ?

771
01:06:37,535 --> 01:06:38,452
Sure .

772
01:06:38,703 --> 01:06:41,622
Does Booth look like Wilbur , or am I crazy ?

773
01:06:41,873 --> 01:06:44,416
Hey , he does a tad with the brush off his lip .

774
01:06:44,668 --> 01:06:48,212
Hair 's different , of course , but the features are something like Patterson 's .

775
01:06:48,463 --> 01:06:52,633
Maybe he looked like Booth . I 've seen dummies that look like people I know .

776
01:06:52,884 --> 01:06:55,219
The caveman is a spitting image of the new commissioner .

777
01:06:55,470 --> 01:06:56,553
Please .

778
01:06:56,805 --> 01:06:58,430
Don 't touch the exhibits .

779
01:06:58,682 --> 01:07:00,557
- Can 't you read the sign ? - I 'm sorry .

780
01:07:00,809 --> 01:07:03,811
Hey , look , where 'd you get the face for this guy that shot Lincoln ?

781
01:07:04,604 --> 01:07:07,523
- From photographs . - Yeah , they take them at that time ?

782
01:07:07,774 --> 01:07:09,191
If you go to the City Library

783
01:07:09,442 --> 01:07:12,695
you 'll find a volume of Mathew Brady 's photos taken during the Civil War .

784
01:07:12,946 --> 01:07:14,738
- Do you work here ? - Yeah .

785
01:07:14,989 --> 01:07:15,823
You make these things ?

786
01:07:16,074 --> 01:07:16,990
Some of them .

787
01:07:17,242 --> 01:07:18,867
What 's your name ?

788
01:07:19,202 --> 01:07:21,412
Leon Averill . What 's yours ?

789
01:07:21,663 --> 01:07:23,831
Jim Shane . I 'm an engineer on the 9th Avenue El .

790
01:07:24,082 --> 01:07:27,501
- It was nice meeting you . - Hm .

791
01:07:29,838 --> 01:07:35,008
Tom , you know me . I 'm no good at names , but I don 't forget faces .

792
01:07:35,260 --> 01:07:38,429
If I can take the muff off of that one , I might be able to place it .

793
01:07:38,680 --> 01:07:40,556
It was a long time ago .

794
01:07:45,228 --> 01:07:46,228
- Mr. Wallace ? - Yes .

795
01:07:46,479 --> 01:07:48,105
I 'm Lieutenant Brennan . Sergeant Shane .

796
01:07:48,356 --> 01:07:50,733
- Glad to know you . Thank you . - Won 't you sit down ?

797
01:07:50,984 --> 01:07:52,901
- Sorry I kept you waiting . - That 's all right .

798
01:07:53,153 --> 01:07:56,405
This is the first time I 've been asked to come to Police Headquarters .

799
01:07:56,656 --> 01:07:58,866
- What am I suspected on ? - Nothing . We thought perhaps ...

800
01:07:59,117 --> 01:08:01,076
- ... you might be able to help us . - Glad to .

801
01:08:01,327 --> 01:08:03,662
We found out that your partner is the same Professor Jarrod

802
01:08:03,913 --> 01:08:06,749
whose museum on 24th Street burned down some time ago .

803
01:08:07,000 --> 01:08:09,001
- That 's true . - Heh .

804
01:08:09,252 --> 01:08:12,921
This , uh , Professor Jarrod was supposed to have been killed in the fire .

805
01:08:13,173 --> 01:08:14,590
Apparently , a slight mistake .

806
01:08:14,841 --> 01:08:16,592
You suspect him of some criminal act ?

807
01:08:16,843 --> 01:08:18,761
- We haven 't a thing on the guy . - We 're curious .

808
01:08:19,012 --> 01:08:20,554
So is the insurance company .

809
01:08:22,056 --> 01:08:23,140
What do you know about his employees ?

810
01:08:23,391 --> 01:08:26,477
There 's Scott Andrews , a protégé of mine .

811
01:08:26,728 --> 01:08:27,770
Yes , we know of him .

812
01:08:28,021 --> 01:08:33,108
Then there 's Igor , deaf-mute , and Leon Averill , who does the wax work .

813
01:08:33,651 --> 01:08:37,321
Averill 's an odd character . Periodical drunkard , but a fine artist .

814
01:08:37,947 --> 01:08:41,200
I 've seen some of his sketches . One of the Savior with his disciples .

815
01:08:41,451 --> 01:08:42,868
Beautiful work .

816
01:08:43,953 --> 01:08:45,287
I 'm afraid I haven 't been much help .

817
01:08:45,538 --> 01:08:48,123
You never can tell . Thank you very much .

818
01:08:48,374 --> 01:08:50,626
- I prefer you not mention this to your partner . - I won 't .

819
01:08:53,046 --> 01:08:55,881
You know , I gamble on Jarrod .

820
01:08:56,132 --> 01:08:59,134
He 's strange , unpredictable , but I think he 's a man of integrity .

821
01:08:59,385 --> 01:09:03,305
- I 'm sure of it . Thank you very much . - Not at all . Good day , gentlemen .

822
01:09:05,225 --> 01:09:07,810
Tom , I told you I knew the man with the whiskers .

823
01:09:08,061 --> 01:09:09,478
Remember that artist in Sing Sing

824
01:09:09,729 --> 01:09:11,814
who painted the Last Supper on the wall of his cell ?

825
01:09:12,065 --> 01:09:15,108
Hendricks . They called him a genius and gave him a parole . Ha , ha !

826
01:09:15,360 --> 01:09:17,694
Yeah , but when they turned him loose , he became a drunk .

827
01:09:17,946 --> 01:09:21,156
He broke parole about a year ago . We 've had him on the wanted list since .

828
01:09:21,407 --> 01:09:23,951
- Carl Hendricks ? - That 's him . Alias Leon Averill .

829
01:09:24,202 --> 01:09:26,495
- Bring him in . - Can do .

830
01:09:58,319 --> 01:10:00,404
Little more bitterness in that face , my boy .

831
01:10:00,947 --> 01:10:03,365
Remember , this fellow has been badly used by the world

832
01:10:03,616 --> 01:10:05,576
and he despises all the people in it .

833
01:10:06,327 --> 01:10:09,580
Deepen those lines around the corner of the mouth .

834
01:10:09,873 --> 01:10:11,540
Not too much .

835
01:10:11,791 --> 01:10:13,917
There . There , that 's better .

836
01:10:14,711 --> 01:10:17,129
What I wouldn 't give to have those fingers of yours .

837
01:10:17,380 --> 01:10:18,463
Thank you , Mr. Jarrod .

838
01:10:18,965 --> 01:10:21,717
Sorry I 've kept you so late here tonight , Scott .

839
01:10:21,968 --> 01:10:22,843
Oh , that 's all right .

840
01:10:23,094 --> 01:10:24,261
Miss Allen is meeting me here .

841
01:10:25,096 --> 01:10:27,806
It 's her birthday . We 're going to celebrate at Chiles ' .

842
01:10:28,057 --> 01:10:28,974
Charming creature .

843
01:10:29,726 --> 01:10:32,269
I was worried about her . The shock of finding that murdered girl ...

844
01:10:32,520 --> 01:10:34,813
- ... gave her some strange ideas . - Yes , I know .

845
01:10:35,064 --> 01:10:37,190
I took her to Brennan at Police Headquarters .

846
01:10:37,442 --> 01:10:40,527
- He set her right . - That 's very good now . Excellent .

847
01:10:40,778 --> 01:10:43,822
Oh , Scott , before you go , would you mind running over to Metzgers for me ?

848
01:10:44,073 --> 01:10:45,824
- Metzgers ? - The place where they make ...

849
01:10:46,075 --> 01:10:47,409
- ... the artificial flowers . - Oh , yes .

850
01:10:47,660 --> 01:10:50,787
They 're doing a background for this new group . Take a look at it for me .

851
01:10:51,039 --> 01:10:53,832
You know what I want . Advise them on the color scheme .

852
01:10:54,083 --> 01:10:57,836
I 'd go myself , but it 's so hard for me to get about .

853
01:10:58,087 --> 01:11:00,672
I know . I 'll be glad to do it . I 'll go right now .

854
01:11:00,924 --> 01:11:02,591
Thank you very much .

855
01:11:07,221 --> 01:11:09,264
I followed him through his bender .

856
01:11:09,515 --> 01:11:13,185
Sometimes , guy gets the shakes so bad , you expect to see his teeth fall out .

857
01:11:13,436 --> 01:11:15,062
- This all he had on him ? - That 's it .

858
01:11:15,313 --> 01:11:16,438
No money ?

859
01:11:20,109 --> 01:11:21,485
Gold .

860
01:11:27,951 --> 01:11:29,743
" To Wilbur Patter- -

861
01:11:31,079 --> 01:11:32,371
Patterson .

862
01:11:32,622 --> 01:11:34,331
With affection and admiration .

863
01:11:34,582 --> 01:11:38,627
City Attorney 's Office . December 25 , 1900 . "

864
01:11:46,094 --> 01:11:48,053
Where did you get this ?

865
01:11:48,304 --> 01:11:49,930
- I found it . - Where ?

866
01:11:50,181 --> 01:11:52,265
- On the El . - What line ?

867
01:11:52,517 --> 01:11:54,768
- Third Avenue , downtown . - When ?

868
01:11:55,019 --> 01:11:57,354
I don 't remember , it was months ago .

869
01:11:58,064 --> 01:12:00,399
- Book him on suspicion of murder . - No . I found that .

870
01:12:00,650 --> 01:12:03,151
I never knew the man who owned it . I never saw him .

871
01:12:03,403 --> 01:12:04,361
Lock him up .

872
01:12:04,612 --> 01:12:07,948
Please don 't put me in a cell . I 'm sick .

873
01:12:08,199 --> 01:12:11,243
Can 't you see my nerves are all shattered ? Look .

874
01:12:11,494 --> 01:12:13,870
Look , please give me one little ... .

875
01:12:15,081 --> 01:12:16,665
Could I have one little drink- - ?

876
01:12:16,916 --> 01:12:21,044
You 're not gonna get anything until you tell us where you got this watch .

877
01:12:24,632 --> 01:12:26,717
- Take him out . - Let 's go .

878
01:13:45,338 --> 01:13:46,505
Scott .

879
01:15:58,512 --> 01:15:59,971
Scott .

880
01:17:29,437 --> 01:17:31,229
You shouldn 't have done that , my dear .

881
01:17:33,357 --> 01:17:34,858
It is Cathy .

882
01:17:35,860 --> 01:17:38,111
It 's Cathy 's body under the wax .

883
01:17:38,362 --> 01:17:40,947
I knew it . I knew it all the time .

884
01:18:06,807 --> 01:18:10,143
Everything I ever loved has been taken away from me .

885
01:18:10,561 --> 01:18:14,314
Not you , my Marie Antoinette , for I will give you eternal life .

886
01:18:42,176 --> 01:18:44,344
This is where I re-created my Joan of Arc .

887
01:18:44,595 --> 01:18:45,929
It 's an interesting process .

888
01:18:46,180 --> 01:18:49,891
If you have patience with me , my dear , I 'll show you how it 's done .

889
01:19:08,786 --> 01:19:13,873
Can 't stand it .

890
01:19:28,806 --> 01:19:30,181
All right .

891
01:19:30,933 --> 01:19:32,517
All right , I 'll tell you what I know .

892
01:19:33,978 --> 01:19:36,187
Patterson was killed because he looked like Booth .

893
01:19:36,439 --> 01:19:37,105
You killed him .

894
01:19:37,356 --> 01:19:39,441
No , not I. Jarrod , at the waxworks .

895
01:19:39,692 --> 01:19:42,068
His hands were no good . He had to take subjects from life .

896
01:19:42,319 --> 01:19:42,986
You helped him ?

897
01:19:43,237 --> 01:19:44,654
No , they were already dead .

898
01:19:44,905 --> 01:19:45,655
What about Burke ?

899
01:19:46,782 --> 01:19:49,409
He 's there too . In wax .

900
01:19:49,660 --> 01:19:52,454
He was the one who set fire to the old museum .

901
01:19:52,830 --> 01:19:54,831
Jarrod came out of it alive , but insane .

902
01:19:55,082 --> 01:19:58,626
- Cathy Gray ? - Joan of Arc . Joan of Arc ! That 's Cathy .

903
01:19:59,253 --> 01:20:02,005
She 's there with all the rest of them . The whole place is a morgue .

904
01:20:02,715 --> 01:20:05,425
He 'll do the same with Sue Allen , if he gets his hands on her .

905
01:20:05,676 --> 01:20:06,801
You 've got to stop him .

906
01:20:07,052 --> 01:20:09,220
You 've got to stop him before he does any more killing .

907
01:20:33,537 --> 01:20:36,122
That look of horror spoils your lovely face .

908
01:20:36,373 --> 01:20:38,875
What if it should show , even through the wax ?

909
01:21:10,115 --> 01:21:18,164
Sue ?

910
01:21:28,634 --> 01:21:30,885
Sue , are you in there ?

911
01:21:37,977 --> 01:21:39,727
Where 's Sue ?

912
01:21:41,105 --> 01:21:42,814
Where is she ? Where is she ?

913
01:23:27,920 --> 01:23:29,629
The end will come quickly , my love .

914
01:23:30,589 --> 01:23:31,756
There 's a pain beyond pain

915
01:23:32,007 --> 01:23:35,551
an agony so intense , it shocks the mind into instant oblivion .

916
01:23:36,220 --> 01:23:37,970
We 'll find immortality together

917
01:23:38,722 --> 01:23:41,349
for they 'll remember me through you .

918
01:24:54,214 --> 01:24:55,757
Where 's Jarrod ?

919
01:24:56,008 --> 01:24:59,302
Where 's Jarrod ? Where 's Jarrod ?

920
01:25:13,525 --> 01:25:16,903
Andrews , where 's Jarrod ?

921
01:25:19,114 --> 01:25:22,116
In the cellar . He 's got Sue .

922
01:25:22,868 --> 01:25:24,452
Take care of him .

923
01:27:14,771 --> 01:27:17,273
The People 's Exhibit Number One .

924
01:27:17,524 --> 01:27:18,691
You almost lost your head , Miss Allen .

925
01:27:18,942 --> 01:27:20,943
Would you care to keep that one as a spare ?

926
01:27:21,194 --> 01:27:22,528
- No , thank you . - Ha-ha-ha .

927
01:27:22,779 --> 01:27:25,615
We 'll never forget you and your men . Thanks to you , we 're still alive .

928
01:27:25,866 --> 01:27:29,493
But every time I shave , I can still feel that guillotine blade .

929
01:27:29,745 --> 01:27:33,122
- Please , let 's not talk about it anymore . - Yes , you 're right .

930
01:27:33,665 --> 01:27:35,291
Mr. Brennan

931
01:27:35,667 --> 01:27:38,210
thank you for the , uh , use of your coat .

932
01:27:38,462 --> 01:27:39,962
Oh ! Oh , that was nothing .

933
01:27:40,213 --> 01:27:41,672
Well , it meant a lot to me .

934
01:27:41,924 --> 01:27:44,675
Well , when I found you weren 't dressed too warmly , I , uh ...

935
01:27:45,260 --> 01:27:46,802
Well , I didn 't want you to catch a cold .

936
01:27:50,307 --> 01:27:51,974
Goodbye , Mr. Brennan , and thanks for everything .

937
01:27:52,601 --> 01:27:53,267
Bye .

938
01:27:54,102 --> 01:27:55,353
Bless you , Mr. Shane .

939
01:27:55,604 --> 01:27:56,562
Thank you , Miss Allen .

940
01:27:58,649 --> 01:28:01,901
You know , Shane , by the time this guy gets out of Sing Sing

941
01:28:02,152 --> 01:28:05,112
this head will grow a long beard .

